commit 3d6bcdfedfcb5b6a298409e249aa52c944dd42b8
Author: Alexander Williams <awill@opentitan.org>
Date:   Tue Apr 2 21:57:10 2024 -0700

    [i2c] Clean up automatic Stop generation and NACK handling

    Consolidate NACK handling events into a single "controller halt" status
    interrupt. The event bits in the CONTROLLER_EVENTS CSR combine to drive
    the interrupt. Clear the bits to acknowledge the interrupt.

    Change up the NACK handling to finish the current byte, force transition
    to the Idle state, and hold there, as well as beginning the timeout
    counter's incrementing there. SCL will be held low if the transaction
    was not stopped already.

    Track automatic Stop generation to eliminate races with software, since
    changes to the control bits could occur while the Stop symbol was being
    generated, leading to a transition to the PopFmtFifo state and the
    discarding of an unused FMT FIFO entry. Proceed directly to Idle if the
    current Stop symbol was automatically generated.

    Signed-off-by: Alexander Williams <awill@opentitan.org>

