commit 7773b039d0db27585b3abb447c0dc64d247eca6d
Author: Alexander Williams <awill@opentitan.org>
Date:   Fri Mar 29 11:46:09 2024 -0700

    [i2c] Split the target and controller FSMs

    Split the target and controller FSMs both to simplify the code for
    better maintainability / readability and to lay the groundwork for
    multi-controller support. Note that there will likely be some increase
    in area for duplicated structures here, but it turns out that much of
    the state was already independent.

    Also fix a bug where the controller-mode stretch counter would continue
    counting cycles even when the target had already released SCL.

    Signed-off-by: Alexander Williams <awill@opentitan.org>

