commit dc9da971498948e75213089c49b7b3d8b45d9567
Author: Michael Schaffner <msf@opentitan.org>
Date:   Wed Aug 9 05:21:00 2023 +0200

    [otp_ctrl] Add option to disable integrity on a partition

    This adds an option to completely disable integrity generation
    and decoding on certain partitions. The partition attribute
    replaces the attribute that did not treat uncorrectable errors
    as fatal. That one got added as a cheap workaround to ensure
    uncorrectable errors do not lead to local escalation on
    some partitions like VENDOR_TEST. Now that we have to support
    thermometer encoded strike counters, we actually need true
    support for disabling integrity since otherwise the data
    would be distorted by the correction mechanism.

    The feature is implemented by adding an additional set of
    commands to the prim_otp wrapper interface that allow
    writing and reading of "RAW" values without added integrity
    and without interpreting the integrity bits.

    Signed-off-by: Michael Schaffner <msf@opentitan.org>

diff --git a/hw/ip/otp_ctrl/dv/env/otp_ctrl_env_pkg.sv b/hw/ip/otp_ctrl/dv/env/otp_ctrl_env_pkg.sv
index 95ca833e10..2073660435 100644
--- a/hw/ip/otp_ctrl/dv/env/otp_ctrl_env_pkg.sv
+++ b/hw/ip/otp_ctrl/dv/env/otp_ctrl_env_pkg.sv
@@ -250,11 +250,10 @@ package otp_ctrl_env_pkg;
