commit eb5ff73f850c8aded0fb372cef6abfc3712b77df
Author: Rupert Swarbrick <rswarbrick@lowrisc.org>
Date:   Thu Apr 13 10:51:28 2023 +0100

    Avoid mutating a global in otbn_tracer.sv

    If you build the previous code with a recent verilator, it complains
    about updating "trace_output_buffer" with a blocking assignment in the
    always block at the bottom of the file. I think it has inferred that
    this block is sequential logic and shouldn't contain blocking
    assignments. Grr!

    This change switches from a mutated global variable to explicitly
    passing the string that we want to update and returning the updated
    value. The end result should be the same.

    Signed-off-by: Rupert Swarbrick <rswarbrick@lowrisc.org>

