dv_diff:
commit 2e9cbc667ac5fafb7805f3a32b63734cfb143fe7
Author: Pirmin Vogel <vogelpi@lowrisc.org>
Date:   Thu Dec 15 16:27:39 2022 +0100

    [kmac] Make masked software keys optional for the unmasked design

    This commit adds a new top-level parameter to KMAC to optionally enable
    masking of the software key in case the unmasked design is chosen. This
    is useful for optionally having fully compatible software interfaces
    between the masked and unmasked design but not unnecessarily inflate the
    area of the unmasked design.

    In case masking is enabled, the parameter has no effect. Software then
    always provides the key in two shares.

    This resolves lowRISC/OpenTitan#16206.

    Signed-off-by: Pirmin Vogel <vogelpi@lowrisc.org>

