commit 0c7a6f3105a6dfff19687e566be5cbe99e9a5ef9
Author: Guillermo Maturana <maturana@google.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 11 16:33:09 2022 -0800

    [dv/pwrmgr] Fix recent unit test failures

    Some of the fixes:

    The change in clock for alert handling being clk_lc rather than clk (and
    the same change for reset) caused the cip scoreboard to loose track of
    alert expectations. Rather than changing cip, this creates a couple of
    functions that enable the pwrmgr to assist cip track resets, and adds
    calls to these in various test sequences.

    The aborted_low_power test was unreliable, so this changes the test to
    rely on internal state machines to determine when to send stimulus and
    to predict expected results.

    Signed-off-by: Guillermo Maturana <maturana@google.com>

