+  // through. Data bits are always left un-modified. A registered version of `locking` is used for
+  // timing reasons. When a read comes in when `locking` has just been asserted, `locking_q` will be
+  // timing reasons. When a read comes in when `locking` has just been asserted, `locking_q` will be
