commit 7245a18ff8705fb9593db0ab9a7985500bdce315
Author: Rupert Swarbrick <rswarbrick@lowrisc.org>
Date:   Tue Jan 25 13:44:27 2022 +0000

    [otbn,dv] Define a new class of trace entry for secure wipe writes

    These appear from the RTL side when secure wipe is enabled and we will
    see each register written with some pseudo-random value and then zero.
    Once everything has been merged, we get something like the following:

        V
        > ACC: 0x00000000_00000000_00000000_00000000_00000000_00000000_00000000_00000000
        > ACC: 0xdf716993_b8b6de41_731c6c2c_ac85a1fc_9ea1db5c_1fc82f0d_ce1f8aeb_318d75a1
        > FLAGS0: {C: 0, M: 0, L: 1, Z: 0}
        > FLAGS1: {C: 0, M: 0, L: 1, Z: 0}
        > MOD: 0x00000000_00000000_00000000_00000000_00000000_00000000_00000000_00000000
        > MOD: 0x5bda6e0a_d54dc0cb_6d4b3ebf_a7cfe0b9_4191b56b_a739d816_ca87dfde_3bad8c9c
        > x02: 0x00000000
        > x02: 0x96ea3fb5
        > x03: 0x00000000
        > x03: 0xd4c44533
        > x04: 0x00000000
        > x04: 0xbea81560
        ...
        > x30: 0x00000000
        > x30: 0xebd16a69
        > x31: 0x00000000
        > x31: 0x2f472790

    This commit doesn't teach the ISS to generate matching entries. Nor
    does it handle the updates above properly: the "concatenate lines and
    then sort" logic can't distinguish between

        x02 <= 0; x02 <= 0x1234

    and

        x02 <= 0x1234; x02 <= 0

    We'll fix that in the next commit.

    Note that there used to be some logic in OtbnTraceChecker::OnIssTrace
    to discard STALL entries with no changes. That was a bit of a hack,
    which I added to avoid breaking things because of some spurious ISS
    STALL lines after the operation had completed. This patch moves the
    "discard STALL" logic to the Python instead which should make things a
    bit easier to debug.

    Signed-off-by: Rupert Swarbrick <rswarbrick@lowrisc.org>

diff --git a/hw/ip/otbn/dv/model/iss_wrapper.cc b/hw/ip/otbn/dv/model/iss_wrapper.cc
