commit 547baf11fca84ce8556ead450234549db8697ee1
Author: Michael Schaffner <msf@opentitan.org>
Date:   Wed Jun 16 18:52:06 2021 -0700

    [lc_ctrl/otp_ctrl] Combine escalation actions 1 and 2

    This simplifies the escalation actions by combining "wipe secrets"
    (which is fanned out into the system via lc_escalate_en) and "lc state
    scrap". This makes implementation and DV easier, since it is difficult
    to logically keep these two actions apart without introducing a whole
    set of unnecessary corner cases. For example, lc_escalate_en basically
    moves all OTP partition controllers into an invalid state. This in turn
    scraps the life cycle state automatically - however, it that one is
    supposed to be a separable action, we need to introduce more logic to
    actually handle that case. In reality, we are already recommending to
    trigger both actions at the same time in the alert handler, so we do not
    really need this separation.

    In terms of implementation, the escalation connections are kept in place
    and are just renamed. That means that we are going to have two
    escalation channels going over to life cycle, and both of them trigger
    the same response (i.e., they become redundant channels). This is not
    unreasonable from a security perspective, and we need to connect the
    unused channel somehow anyways to keep the ping mechanism alive.

    Signed-off-by: Michael Schaffner <msf@opentitan.org>

